#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
#  tuisla — A Tesla TUI
#
#  USAGE:  python3 tuisla [--mode MODE] [--unit UNIT] [--refresh S] [--invert]
#                         [--simple] [--bw]
#          python3 tuisla -l|--login            (both steps below)
#          python3 tuisla --login-tesla [--print]
#          python3 tuisla --login-mtm
#          python3 tuisla --setup-vc
#
#  LOGIN:  --login-tesla signs in to Tesla in the browser and saves a refresh
#          token to $XDG_STATE_HOME/tuisla/refresh_token (~/.local/state/...),
#          mode 600.  tuisla keeps that file up to date when Tesla rotates the
#          token.  --print writes the token to stdout instead of saving it.
#          --login-mtm opens MyTeslaMate (API tab: allow commands for the
#          vehicle, copy the MyTeslaMate API token, not the Fleet API one) and
#          asks for that token (Enter skips); saved as .../myteslamate_token.
#
#  MODES:  Vehicle data is read from the Tesla Owner API; the mode only
#          decides where commands go.
#    ro    Read-only: commands are checked but not sent (dry run).  A valid
#          command shows "✓ ... (ro: not sent)"; malformed ones still fail.
#          Demo mode (no Tesla token) dry-runs commands the same way.
#    mtm   (default) Commands go to MyTeslaMate (api.myteslamate.com) using the
#          MyTeslaMate token.  The Tesla token is not sent to them.
#    vc    Commands are signed with your own key, paired with the car, by
#          Tesla's tesla-http-proxy (teslamotors/vehicle-command), which tuisla
#          starts by itself, and go to the Fleet API with a token from your own
#          Tesla developer app.  --setup-vc walks through all of it.  Without
#          an Owner API login, vehicle data is read from the Fleet API too
#          (billed by Tesla, so refreshing every 60 s at most).
#
#  UNITS:  metric | us (temperatures typed in commands follow the unit)
#
#  ENV:
#    TESLA_REFRESH_TOKEN    Optional. Used instead of the saved token if set.
#                           Without any token tuisla runs in demo mode.
#    TESLA_VIN              Optional. Pin to a specific vehicle; by default the
#                           first vehicle on the account is used.
#    MYTESLAMATE_TOKEN      Optional. Used instead of the saved MyTeslaMate
#                           token if set; mtm needs one or the other.
#    VEHICLE_COMMAND_URL    Optional. A tesla-http-proxy you run yourself for vc
#                           mode (e.g. https://localhost:4443) instead of the
#                           one tuisla starts.
#    VEHICLE_COMMAND_CERT   CA file for that proxy's TLS cert. Default: cert.pem
#                           (relative to the current directory)
# =============================================================================

